  "body": "Part of #308. Depends on #316 (setup transform) and #317 (carried body).\n\n## Proposal\n- Per setup, a user parameter **Stock: New block / From previous setup** (CAM choices are user parameters with a default): default *From previous setup* for setup 2+ once a transform is set, *New block* otherwise; an undoable command; saved.\n- The Setup page shows the incoming stock (the carried body, transformed) in the viewport and names the setup it comes from; the setup sheet lists it.\n- Prerequisite UX: #45 (a new document cannot create its first setup from the UI).\n\nPrior art (behaviour only, public docs): CAM systems expose this as \"stock from preceding setup\" plus a \"continue rest machining\" switch, and warn that the displayed in-process stock can be stale until the earlier setup is re-simulated.\n\n## Done means\nThe parameter round-trips (save/load, undo/redo); switching it marks the setup's ops Stale; the viewport and setup sheet show the incoming stock (UI test).\n",
